  "reason": "The study investigates MPXV in pets of human cases but does not report a quantitative measure of agreement between animal and human clinical results. It focuses on detecting MPXV DNA and antibodies in animals and environmental samples, and while it notes a correlation in cycle threshold values between animal/environmental DNA and human DNA, this is framed as evidence of contamination rather than a measure of translational agreement."
